---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Contribute | Macro Evidence"
  description="Contribute code, documentation, issues, and other improvements to Macro Evidence through clear repository-owned paths."
>
  <PageIntro
    kicker="Contribute"
    title="Build with us."
    lead="We welcome thoughtful contributions to our software, documentation, and public infrastructure. Start with the repository that owns the work, and talk with us before investing significant time in a large change."
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="site-container split">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Before you start</span>
        <h2>
          Small fixes can start small. Large changes should start with scope.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="reading">
        <p>
          Small, self-contained fixes may be proposed directly where the
          affected repository's guidance permits. For a large change, new
          dependency, architectural change, or public-interface change, open an
          issue first so the scope can be discussed before substantial work
          begins.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section records-section">
    <div class="site-container split">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">How we review contributions</span>
        <h2>Acceptance is selective and evidence-based.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          We may accept, decline, request changes to, or defer proposed work
          based on factors including:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>fit with current repository scope and needs;</li>
          <li>technical or editorial merit and appropriate evidence;</li>
          <li>
            maintainability and consistency with architecture and standards;
          </li>
          <li>security and operational risk;</li>
          <li>licensing and third-party provenance;</li>
          <li>governance alignment;</li>
          <li>review capacity and long-term maintenance cost.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Meeting one factor does not guarantee acceptance.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="site-container split">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Contributor rights</span>
        <h2>Review and merge are separate gates.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="reading">
        <p>
          External copyrightable contributions may be opened and reviewed, but
          they are not merged until the applicable contributor-agreement
          requirement is satisfied.
        </p>
        <p class="reference-context">
          The full policy and Code of Conduct below are maintained on GitHub.
        </p>
        <div class="reference-links">
          <a
            class="text-link"
            href="https://github.com/macro-evidence/governance/blob/main/CONTRIBUTION_POLICY.md"
          >
            Read the Contribution Policy →
          </a>
          <a
            class="text-link"
            href="https://github.com/macro-evidence/.github/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md"
          >
            Read the Code of Conduct →
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section engage-band">
    <div class="site-container split">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Where to start</span>
        <h2>Find the repository that owns the work.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="reading">
        <p>
          Repository-specific setup, architecture, and technical requirements
          stay with the repository itself. If you are unsure where an idea
          belongs, ask before investing significant time.
        </p>
        <p class="reference-context">
          The organization guidance and repository list below open on GitHub.
        </p>
        <div class="reference-links">
          <a
            class="text-link"
            href="https://github.com/macro-evidence/.github/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md"
          >
            Read organization contribution guidance →
          </a>
          <a
            class="text-link"
            href="https://github.com/orgs/macro-evidence/repositories"
          >
            Browse repositories →
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
